  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 128 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nModel discrepancy leads to a low probability forecast as we head \ninto the early portions of Thanksgiving week. The highest confidence \nfor next week is that it will be cold with forecast pcpn amounts \nbeing very light through TX Panhandle. The 12Z GFS is wanting to \nmove some light snow into west TX Tuesday afternoon but as was \nmentioned above that currently is a very low probability scenario. \nWhat does appear likely is there will be several shortwave's moving \nthrough the flow across the western and southwestern US next week \nand the evolution of these will eventually determine what the \neffects on our sensible weather will be.",
